(Eq.~\ref{eq:tstar}): a matched-filter amplitude divided by a noise
estimate. Dimensionless, and \emph{not} quoted in units of $\sigma$,
its null distribution being neither assumed nor shown to be Gaussian \\
$T_{\rm trig}$ & the trigger, $T_{\rm trig}=\StageNullTrig$: a fixed level
on $T_\star$, not a tail probability. Throughout, $\sigma$ is reserved for
