Every EIRP quoted here is the \emph{total} radiated power of an unresolved
monochromatic carrier, not the power falling in the peak ALMA channel \\
$P_{50}$, $P_{90}$ & the injected amplitudes the \emph{trigger} recovers half
and nine-tenths of the time, $\PNinetyOverTrig\,P_{\rm eff}$ at 90 per cent:
completeness of one stage, not of the selection
(\S\ref{sec:dwell}, Appendix~\ref{app:inject}) \\
$P_{90}^{\rm sel}$ & the amplitude the complete automated selection recovers
nine-tenths of the time, trigger \emph{and} control-ring gate together
(\S\ref{sec:pninetysel}): the headline sensitivity, in which every limit in
the abstract, discussion and conclusions is expressed \\
Class~A/B & fine-channel / coarse-channel windows; different experiments,
never pooled in a completeness statement (\S\ref{sec:method},
Table~\ref{tab:specclass}) \\
dwell & recovery against the fraction of the track a signal is present
(\S\ref{sec:dwell}) \\
candidate & a stage-1 flagged window that also recurs or is independently
confirmed; this survey reports none (\S\ref{sec:statistic}) \\
pseudo-star & an inner-annulus control probe ranked against the others; it
contains no star, so a first rank is a false alarm by construction
(\S\ref{sec:radial}) \\
debit $m(0)$ & the radial correction subtracted from the stellar statistic
before ranking (\S\ref{sec:radial}) \\
stratum & a subset of windows sharing an instrumental property (band, array,
channelisation) analysed separately (Appendix~\ref{app:inject}) \\
ring max & the largest control statistic in a window's annulus
(\S\ref{sec:statistic}) \\
$R_\sigma$ & the star's robust residual scale over the controls' median;
unity means no noise peculiar to the stellar position (\S\ref{sec:rsigma}) \\
hold-out & blocks withheld from the analysis by a rule fixed in advance, used
only to check a threshold and never to set one (\S\ref{sec:heldout}) \\
drift & the rate at which a carrier's observed frequency changes,
$\dot\nu=\nu a/c$ for line-of-sight acceleration $a$. Quoted in
Hz\,s$^{-1}$ or kHz\,s$^{-1}$ for one window, and in
Hz\,s$^{-1}$\,GHz$^{-1}$ ($=\dot\nu/\nu$, so $a/c$) where a statement is
meant to hold across bands; 1\,Hz\,s$^{-1}$\,GHz$^{-1}$ is
$10^{-9}$\,s$^{-1}$, or $0.30$\,m\,s$^{-2}$ (\S\ref{sec:frames}) \\
add-one rank & the star's rank among $\NCtrl+1$ positions, defined so that
rank-first gives $1/(\NCtrl+1)$ rather than zero: a screening resolution,
not a false-alarm probability (\S\ref{sec:statistic}) \\
crossing & one channel$\times$drift cell at the stellar position with
$T\geq5$ (state 1); counted per window in the main text and per cell in
Appendix~\ref{app:falsealarm} \\
