\emph{resolution} of one window's control ensemble, the smallest per-window
probability the design can express, and not an attainable false-alarm
probability, the controls being only approximately exchangeable with the
star (\S\ref{sec:radial}) \\
$P(\text{false trigger})$ & the survey-level false-positive probability
after thresholding, correlation and non-Gaussianity: a property of the whole
survey, where $p_{\rm rank,min}$ is a property of one window's ensemble. The
survey-wide Bonferroni scale $\BonfScaleCalc$ lies a factor \BonfRankRatio{}
below it (\S\ref{sec:technosearch}) \\
work-list complete & every star on the frozen candidate work list of
\S\ref{sec:sample} that proves genuinely covered is searched. Not
``target-complete'' or ``archive-complete'': neither every ALMA-observed star
within 40\,pc nor all available data are searched. Paired as ``work-list
complete but epoch-incomplete'' \\
epoch-incomplete & \NEB{} of the \NProgenitorEBTotal{} public execution blocks
those targets hold are in this release (\S\ref{sec:sample}) \\
\hline
