Bottom: the same correlation correction applied to the control maxima, which
are measured in the same units and calibrate the budget empirically.}
\label{tab:excess}
\begin{tabular}{@{}P{0.60\columnwidth}rr@{}}
\hline
Quantity & Value & Factor \\
\hline
On-star cells $\geq T_{\rm trig}$ & \CellsObserved & \\
\quad in the stage-1 windows & \CellsObsFlagged & \\
\quad remaining, unattributed & \CellsObsRest & \\
iid-Gaussian expectation (cells) & \CellExpect & \CellsRestOverExpect \\
\hline
Cells per crossing window (obs./exp.) & \CellsPerCrossObs/\CellsPerCrossExp &
\CellsPerCrossRatio \\
\quad predicted by Hanning correlation & \FaFreqOver & \\
Crossing windows (obs./exp.) & \NHitWindowsRest/\ExpCrossWin &
\CrossWinRatio \\
\quad one-sided Poisson $p$ & \CrossWinPoisson & \\
\hline
