\subsection{The $\beta$~Pictoris frame audit}

Table~\ref{tab:bpicaudit} carries the frame chain for the line-attributed
windows: frequencies match the catalogued rest values to the chain's stated
tolerance, velocities are concordant across epochs and transitions, the
emission localises against the control ensemble, and the drift class is zero
to within the grid. Two further properties fit CO and not a carrier. The
stage-1 Band~6 window carries \NCrossBpicSix{} threshold crossings where a
channel-confined carrier admits one, a floor of \BpWidthSixKms\,km\,s$^{-1}$
on the feature's extent; and the peak flux densities, \FluxBpicThree{} and
\FluxBpicSix\,mJy per channel, are the right order for this belt's spatially
integrated CO, their ratio depressed below optically thin LTE by beam dilution
on emission resolved in both beams and by the subthermal excitation of
\citet{Matra2017}.

Stellar emission, the competing explanation towards an active young star, is
suppressed twice: chromospheric and coronal gyrosynchrotron and free-free
emission are broadband --- the AU~Mic flares of \citet{MacGregor2020} are
coherent across the full 8\,GHz --- whereas the block-median baseline of
\S\ref{sec:statistic} removes everything broader than its \MedWin-channel
passband (${\sim}32$\,MHz at the fine class), and the inverse-variance stack
over all integrations dilutes time-confined flares. What survives is the
multiplicative route of \S\ref{sec:statistic}, a flare continuum times a
spectral calibration residual, bounded there and measured for CP$-$72~2713 in
\S\ref{sec:technosearch}.

The carbon tuning agrees by omission. All \NBandEightWin{} Band~8 windows
belong to \BandEightStars{} stars and are [C\,\textsc{i}]
$^{3}P_{1}$--$^{3}P_{0}$ (\MaskCIGHz\,GHz) tunings. HD~48370's on-star
crossing reaches $T_\star=5.05$ against a ring maximum of 6.23 and lies
\CIcrossKms\,km\,s$^{-1}$ from [C\,\textsc{i}], so it is an ordinary noise
crossing and the window shows no line at the star in this disc's carbon
tuning, as \citet{Cataldi2023} report. The crossing peak in the flagged window
is $\FluxHdFour$\,Jy in one 122-kHz channel, with the ring at the same
level.

